# MOVE-AND-KEEP variant of smoke-2x-D.env, About-dialog target (see that file for the full
# field-by-field rationale, repeated below only where it differs). The twin of
# smoke-2x-D-move-keep-notepad.env: same form, other style row. The route-B table has two style
# rows -- THICKFRAME (notepad) and non-THICKFRAME (the About dialog) -- and MoveResizeTarget.lock
# locks ONE window per run, so the two rows are two runs.
#
# HOW THE ABOUT DIALOG BECOMES THE MOVE TARGET: by leaving MOVE_TARGET EMPTY. An empty (or
# absent) filter is the harness's historical About heuristic -- `MoveResizeTarget.matches(title:
# filter: nil)` -- which locks the newest About-shaped window, i.e. the one this run's own base
# app (winver, WINDOW_SMOKE_APP's default) just opened. That is the same mechanism every
# pre-MOVE_TARGET run used, and the reason the notepad-targeted jobs have to NAME notepad: an
# explicit filter can never lock the base app's own window, only a window that appeared after the
# extra apps launched. Not a title match on the About dialog, which is exactly what the record
# convention forbids.
#
# EXTRA_APPS STAYS notepad even though notepad is not the target here: the move/resize scenario's
# own multi-window prerequisite is EXTRA_APPS, not the filter (main.swift's
# `moveResizeScenarioEnabled` doc comment), and the run is not judgeable without it.
#
# Differences from smoke-2x-D.env, and nothing else: TAG, BATCH, MOVE_KEEP=1, an EMPTY
# MOVE_TARGET, and REQUIRE_SYMBOL.
# One window-smoke run in the W3 2x checkpoint's SHAPE 2 form: an exact-2x display, the product
# default advertisement, and the notepad + MOVE leg. Consumed by smoke-job.command (via
# `run-scenario.sh smoke 2x-D`), never by relay.command: it carries no PROGRAM and opens no
# redirected drive.
#
# This is the tracked form of what .build/lab-runtime/c2p-run2.command was on 2026-09-09 -- the
# run the checkpoint record files as "跑 2 (产品默认 D)". Everything that was hand-written in that
# file is a VALUE here; the two refuse-to-run preflight gates it carried are the wrapper's, and
# turning either of them off is a matter of clearing a key rather than deleting a line of code.
#
# TAG names smoke-<TAG>.log (the wrapper's own, polled by checkpoint.sh) and
# window-smoke-<TAG>.log (the run's evidence, under .build/evidence/<BATCH>/).
TAG=2xD-mkeep-about

# The evidence directory this run's log lands in. It names the LANE, not the date: a dated run
# name is given on the command line instead (`run-scenario.sh smoke 2x-D checkpoint-20260910`, or
# checkpoint.sh's own second argument), which run-scenario.sh appends to the RUNTIME copy of this
# file. That is deliberate -- a tracked definition should not have to be edited to run it twice.
BATCH=w3-routeb-wiring

# PREFLIGHT 1 (the display). Exact 2x: a QHD panel set to "looks like 1280 x 720", so the session
# desktop is 1280x720 pt x rasterScale 2 = 2560x1440 remote px. The wrapper refuses unless
# `system_profiler SPDisplaysDataType` reports `UI Looks like: 1280 x 720`. This is not a nicety:
# every remote-pixel number the run produces is judged against that geometry, and on any other
# display the run is unjudgeable rather than merely different. Clear the key to skip the check.
DISPLAY_LOOKS_LIKE=1280x720

# What this run advertises in TS_UD_CS_CORE (ADR-0018 §2 lane E). D = the PRODUCT DEFAULT, which
# the wrapper expresses by leaving WINDOW_SMOKE_ADVERTISED_SCALE unset -- exactly what the
# 2026-09-09 run 2 did with `unset WINDOW_SMOKE_ADVERTISED_SCALE`, and what makes this run a
# measurement of the shipping default rather than of a fixture knob. The sibling forms are `none`
# (the explicit off switch), `DD` (the U-1 control) and an explicit `<desktop>[,<device>]` pair.
#
# D IS THE ONE VALUE OF THIS KEY THAT DOES NOT REACH THE CHILD. The other three are passed through
# verbatim as WINDOW_SMOKE_ADVERTISED_SCALE; D removes the variable instead. That inverts the
# spelling main.swift uses -- there, an unset knob is the product default and the literal string "D"
# is a fixture proposal -- and it is deliberate: a job file says what the run ADVERTISES, and the
# product default is not something a fixture turns on. The consequence to know about is that the
# fixture's own D proposal cannot be requested through this wrapper at all; a job that needs it has
# to say `DD` (the U-1 control) or an explicit pair.
ADVERTISED_SCALE=D

# The scenario legs. MOVE needs the multi-window prerequisite, which EXTRA_APPS provides.
# MOVE_TARGET is DELIBERATELY EMPTY here -- empty means "no filter", which is the harness's
# About heuristic, which is how this run targets the About dialog (see the header). Empty, not
# absent, for the same reason smoke-1x-D.env writes an empty DISPLAY_LOOKS_LIKE: the key is
# present so the file SAYS the emptiness is a choice, and the offline suite's tracked-job
# traversal admits a MOVE=1 job with no filter only when the key is written out.
MOVE=1
MAXIMIZE=0
TRAY=0
TRAY_CLICK=0
EXTRA_APPS=notepad
MOVE_TARGET=

# MOVE_KEEP=1 (WINDOW_SMOKE_MOVE_KEEP): suppress the move/resize scenario's SC_CLOSE of the locked
# target -- both of its close sites, the round end and the rounds-stopped exit a K > 1 run can take
# -- and nothing else: every leg still runs and still reports its verdict, the window is simply
# left open at the end so a host-side probe run afterwards, in the same logged-on session, can read
# its rectangles. Absent or 0 is the unconditional close every other job gets.
#
# The consequence to plan for: this run does NOT clean up after itself. The orchestration logs off
# between runs (jobs/logoff-path.env), which is what disposes of the kept window.
MOVE_KEEP=1

# EDGE_PROFILE (registered here, deliberately NOT set). 1 puts WINDOW_SMOKE_EDGE_PROFILE=1 in the
# child, which makes window-smoke print one measurement-only `[edge]` line per window per sample
# point -- the O-A edge/corner border profile read straight out of the displayed IOSurface (ADR-0018
# §5.1 增补 2026-09-10, About-offset survey §5 (f)). It measures and asserts nothing: no verdict, no
# effect on the exit code, no image written. Absent (as here) or 0 leaves the knob unset, so THIS
# run stays byte-comparable with the 2026-09-09 run it is the tracked form of. A run that wants the
# profile says so in its own job file rather than by editing this one -- which is also what makes
# "was the diagnostic armed" answerable from a job file afterwards instead of from a shell history.
#
# PREFLIGHT 2 (the checkout). The knob this run is NAMED for must exist in the tree that is about
# to be built -- here MOVE_KEEP's own, not the advertisement's. Without this gate a checkout that
# predates the keep knob builds cleanly, runs cleanly, closes the target at the end, and produces
# a log that looks exactly like a run of smoke-2x-D.env -- because it is one, and nothing in the
# evidence says so. The other half -- that the two close sites actually consult the knob -- is held
# by the CALL-SITE pins in Scripts/test-window-smoke-pins.sh: the fixture's own self-test can pin
# the knob's DECISION offline but cannot enter a live close site.
REQUIRE_SYMBOL=WINDOW_SMOKE_MOVE_KEEP
